🟡 **Medium** `src/index.css:1082`

The media query at `max-width: 39.999rem` applies the 16px font-size floor on any narrow window, not just phones. Because `rem` is relative to the interface font size, a 20px root font turns this threshold into ~800px, so a desktop window narrower than that silently ignores any selected prompt font size of 12–15px and forces 16px instead. The phone focus-zoom workaround has no benefit on desktop browsers, so consider gating this with a pointer or hover media feature (e.g. `@media (max-width: 39.999rem) and (pointer: coarse)`) so the floor only applies on touch devices.

```suggestion
@media (max-width: 39.999rem) and (pointer: coarse) {
  .composer-editor-surface {
    font-size: max(var(--font-size-prompt, 1rem), 16px);
  }
}
```

<details>
<summary>🤖 Copy this <strong>AI Prompt</strong> to have your agent fix this:</summary>

