`src/themePalette.ts:812`

`ThemeLibraryStorageError` derives its `message` from `cause.message`, and `cause` is its only field, so the error carries no stable structural context. Consider capturing the storage key (the only variable context at the failure site) and deriving the message from it, keeping the original failure only as `cause` — this matches `ThemeStorageError` in `hooks/useTheme.ts`.

```diff
 export class ThemeLibraryStorageError extends Schema.TaggedErrorClass<ThemeLibraryStorageError>()(
   "ThemeLibraryStorageError",
-  { cause: Schema.Defect() },
+  { storageKey: Schema.String, cause: Schema.Defect() },
 ) {
   override get message(): string {
-    return `Could not save the theme library. ${this.cause instanceof Error ? this.cause.message : "Storage is unavailable."}`;
+    return `Could not save the theme library to ${this.storageKey}.`;
   }
 }
```

