https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/blob/cfb5bacb1af1eaf72d3b1381e6fb8441d9346e67/apps/mobile/src/features/threads/thread-work-log.tsx#L192-L209

`collapsedWorkLogHeight` computes the collapsed group height from every activity row plus a header, but when a group has overflow the component only renders the final `MAX_VISIBLE_WORK_LOG_ENTRIES` row (1) and an overflow toggle button. The returned height therefore covers all rows while only one row plus the toggle is rendered, so the virtual list gets a fixed size that doesn't match the actual content — causing incorrect scroll offsets and visible jump corrections when the row is measured. The toggle height needs to be included and the row count clamped to match `visibleRows`.

