🟡 **Medium** `settings/SettingsPanels.tsx:1529`

After a settings-search jump to a legacy row, the user can collapse the section and trigger the same search again, but the section stays collapsed and the target row remains hidden. `lastExpandedTargetRef` is only ever set to the current `searchTargetId` and never reset, so on the second jump the guard `lastExpandedTargetRef.current === searchTargetId` short-circuits before `setOpen(true)` runs. Consider clearing `lastExpandedTargetRef.current` back to `null` when `searchTargetId` becomes `null` so each new search jump re-expands the section.

```diff
  useEffect(() => {
+    if (searchTargetId === null) {
+      lastExpandedTargetRef.current = null;
+      return;
+    }
    if (!LEGACY_FEATURE_TARGET_IDS.has(searchTargetId)) return;
    if (lastExpandedTargetRef.current === searchTargetId) return;
```

