`decodeScanCache` accepts a cache whose interned `models` array contains non-strings (e.g. `models: [1]`). When a row references index 0, the guard `model === undefined` passes because `models[0]` is `1`, so the entry is installed as a warm cache hit. Later, `UsageAggregator.add` passes the numeric `record.model` to `normalizeModelName`, which calls `model.trim()` and crashes the usage read. Validate that every element of `models` and `sessions` is a string before using them, and reject the cache when any is not.
