🟡 **Medium** `components/RightPanelTabs.tsx:283`

`focusOnMount` is an inline arrow function, so it gets a new identity on every render and React treats it as a changed callback ref — detaching and reattaching it each time, which calls `node.focus()` repeatedly. Any state or prop update (e.g. a `liveAgentCount` badge change) refocuses the launcher container and can yank focus away from a card the user tabbed to. Moving the focus into a mount-only `useEffect` would run it exactly once.

